  callers="CALLERS: `verifyAnchorsDbReady` has one caller, the boot `Promise.all(...).catch` in originate `index.ts` (it logs and carries on); `getAnchorByDocumentId` has one caller, the GET /:documentId route, whose catch answers the constant 500 (KS-1657: a failed read is never a 404). WHAT AN ORDINARY ERROR GETS (the rule for taking the site): the lookup logs one warn line and rethrows the original value; the route logs one error line and answers the constant 500 INTERNAL_ERROR; `verifyAnchorsDbReady` logs one error line and throws the constant `Database is required for anchor operations`. Today (hostile non-string message, real winston): the GET still answers 500 but the warn line is lost and the error line carries the logger's own error text; `verifyAnchorsDbReady` rejects with the logger's error instead of the constant. After: the ordinary rows with the constant in each line. Persisted state: nothing is written either way. **BEHAVIOUR CHANGE the raise PR must state (TIER 1, anchoring):** for an Error with a readable-but-hostile non-string message only, `verifyAnchorsDbReady` rejects with the constant error and both GET lines are logged; the status never changes; a Symbol message is logged as its text; every string message and every non-Error throw behave exactly as before. One edge: an Error whose own message is `undefined` was logged with no `error` value and is now logged as the text 'undefined'.",
  ncells='12 cells: C1 to C4 controls, R1 to R8 red',
